,"license":"Elsevier TDM","accessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.1016/j.agwat.2021.107063"],"publicationDate":"2021-10-01","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"issn___print::258a378f6795ec3fbe5806e6b0fa6835","value":"Agricultural Water Management"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.agwat.2021.107063"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"3179309142"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.agwat.2021.107063"],"refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::5f532a3fc4f1ea403f37070f59a7a53a","value":"Microsoft Academic Graph"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.agwat.2021.107063"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.1016/j.agwat.2021.107063","https://hal.inrae.fr/hal-03769814v1"],"publicationDate":"2021-01-01","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::c7a9f13a6c0940277d46706c7ca32601","value":"HAL INRAE"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::c7a9f13a6c0940277d46706c7ca32601","value":"HAL INRAE"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.agwat.2021.107063"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/https://doi.org/10.1016/j.agwat.2021.107063"],"publicationDate":"2021-10-01","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::b710915795b9e9c02cf10d6d2bdb688c","value":"Institut National de la Recherche Agronomique: ProdINRA"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::df45502607927471ecf8a6ae83683ff5","value":"Bielefeld Academic Search Engine (BASE)"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"3179309142"},{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.1016/j.agwat.2021.107063"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.agwat.2021.107063"],"refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::5f532a3fc4f1ea403f37070f59a7a53a","value":"Microsoft Academic Graph"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::7645a724488c423ea4d1ab803244ba4e","fullName":"Somayyeh Razzaghi","name":"Somayyeh","surname":"Razzaghi","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-8028-452x"},"provenance":null}}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":[{"code":"TR","label":"Turkey","provenance":null}],"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Soil water deficit;Bread wheat;Assimilate remobilization;Photosynthesis;Yield components"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0401 agriculture, forestry, and fisheries"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Soil Sciences and Ecology"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"04 agricultural and veterinary sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Toprak Bilimi ve Ekolojisi"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Soil moisture deficit drives assimilate remobilization and grain yield variability in bread wheat genotypes","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p xml:lang=\"en\">Soil moisture deficit and drought, exacerbated by climate change, frequently affect crop yields. This study aimed to evaluate the physiological and agronomic responses of bread wheat (Triticum aestivum L.) genotypes under soil moisture deficit conditions. Field experiments were conducted using a randomized complete block design during the 2015–2016 growing season at the Agricultural and Natural Resources Research Station in southwestern West Azerbaijan Province, Iran. The study treatments were full irrigation and irrigation cutoff at the flowering stage with seven bread wheat genotypes and the Orum, Zare, Zarin, and Mihan cultivars. The bread wheat grain yield and its components, and some physiological traits like the contribution of photosynthesis, assimilate remobilization, and harvest index (HI) were determined in this study. A significant reduction was observed in yield components (spikelets/spike, grains/spike, grain weight/spike, and spike weight) under drought stress. The Mihan cultivar exhibited the highest spikelets/spike (15), grains/spike (38), grain weight/spike (1.62 g), and spike weight (2.17 g). The intensification of drought stress increased the contribution of remobilization of stored assimilates by 25%. The Mihan cultivar had the highest remobilization rate at 52%, while line C-91-7 and line C-91-5 had the lowest at 27 %. The HI decreased by 20% under soil water deficient stress. The Mihan cultivar, with a HI of 50%, and C-91-8, with 41%, had the highest and lowest HI, respectively. The mean comparison of the contribution of the current photosynthesis trait to wheat grain yield from full irrigation to severe water shortage dropped to 41.2%. Under full irrigation and irrigation cutoff conditions, line C-91-4 had the highest grain yield, with 8747 kg/ha and 5039 kg/ha, respectively. Furthermore, the highest grain yield under full irrigation and irrigation cutoff treatment was related to the Mihan cultivar, with 7569 kg/ha and 4856 kg/ha. Based on these findings, the Mihan cultivar and C-91-4 line are recommended for cultivation in semi-arid regions facing water limitations. Understanding physiological traits and yield components is critical for selecting drought-tolerant wheat varieties in the context of climate change.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2025-06-26","publisher":"International Journal of Agriculture Environment and Food Sciences","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref","Volume: 9, Issue: 2529-538","2618-5946","International Journal of Agriculture Environment and Food Sciences"],"formats":["application/pdf"],"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"International Journal of Agriculture Environment and Food Sciences","issnPrinted":null,"issnOnline":"2618-5946","issnLinking":null,"ep":"538","iss":null,"sp":"529","vol":"9","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::7dd13af8686d0392d1e943aeab92d96e","originalIds":["10.31015/2025.2.26","50|doiboost____|7dd13af8686d0392d1e943aeab92d96e","91df77e3-ddcd-4e61-a405-e3c0b5aad9d0","50|od______9447::954cf3443ed77a16ccbaf27b3cd59ea6","50|tubitakulakb::72e790dd418e05c3e18baf120ab12e16","oai:dergipark.org.tr:article/1669967"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.31015/2025.2.26"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":1.0,"influence":2.2121218E-9,"popularity":2.8932239E-9,"impulse":1.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Erciyes University","acronym":"Erciyes University","id":"openorgs____::50ff920e3f2baaa9d847e091109b5328","pids":[{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000123312603"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"87673952"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100016209"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100016209"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/047g8vk19"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.411739.9"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q4810943"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"3748597"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"996573830"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100003062"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q4810943"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100003062"},{"scheme":"OrgReg","value":"TR0038"}],"countries":[{"code":"TR","label":"Turkey"}],"websiteurl":"http://en.erciyes.edu.tr/"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"opendoar____::22456f4b545572855c766df5eefc9832","value":"Erciyes University - AVESIS"},{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"},{"key":"openaire____::85e51732975595215ae3c2514e272ce6","value":"TÜBİTAK ULAKBİM DergiPark"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.31015/2025.2.26"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.31015/2025.2.26"],"publicationDate":"2025-06-26","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"doajarticles::e13a9ffb461e15b114a5861bdedacf4c","value":"International Journal of Agriculture, Environment and Food Sciences"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.31015/2025.2.26"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_14cb","label":"CLOSED","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["https://avesis.erciyes.edu.tr/publication/details/91df77e3-ddcd-4e61-a405-e3c0b5aad9d0/oai"],"publicationDate":"2025-06-01","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::22456f4b545572855c766df5eefc9832","value":"Erciyes University - AVESIS"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::22456f4b545572855c766df5eefc9832","value":"Erciyes University - AVESIS"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.31015/2025.2.26"}],"type":"Article","urls":["https://dergipark.org.tr/tr/pub/jaefs/issue/91914/1669967"],"publicationDate":"2025-04-04","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::85e51732975595215ae3c2514e272ce6","value":"TÜBİTAK ULAKBİM DergiPark"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::85e51732975595215ae3c2514e272ce6","value":"TÜBİTAK ULAKBİM DergiPark"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Mohamed Emran","name":"Mohamed","surname":"Emran","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::27c0615b0e4bb88bae14b1c7a5678392","fullName":"Omar M. Ibrahim","name":"Omar M.","surname":"Ibrahim","rank":2,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-3439-9155"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Asal M. Wali","name":"Asal M.","surname":"Wali","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Khaled M. Darwish","name":"Khaled M.","surname":"Darwish","rank":4,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::08d3429e4fcfc4a8350112a61906b46f","fullName":"Rasha M. Badr Eldin","name":"Rasha M.","surname":"Badr Eldin","rank":5,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0001-6886-1390"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::9eefb30bced125996e52de5998f38923","fullName":"Maryam M. Alomran","name":"Maryam M.","surname":"Alomran","rank":6,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0001-9410-9792"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Amira M. El-Tahan","name":"Amira M.","surname":"El-Tahan","rank":7,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid_pending","value":"0000-0002-0316-1948"},"provenance":null}}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0301 basic medicine"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"2. Zero hunger"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0303 health sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"wheat production"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"drought stress"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"supplemental irrigation"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Botany"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"15. Life on land"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Article"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"6. Clean water"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"03 medical and health sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"arid lands"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"calcareous soil"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"QK1-989"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"silicon foliar application"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Assessing Soil Quality, Wheat Crop Yield, and Water Productivity under Condition of Deficit Irrigation","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Wheat is one of the most important cereal crops in Egypt and all over the world. Its productivity is adversely affected by drought due to deficient irrigation to provide nutrients required for plant growth. In a field experiment, silicon foliar applications at concentrations of 0, 200, and 400 mg L−1 were performed at different irrigation rates ranging from 1000 to 4000 m3 ha−1 to assess water irrigation productivity and wheat crop yield in a calcareous soil under arid climate conditions. Increased irrigation rates led to a significant increase in soil nutrient dynamics, as well as in the number and weight of grains per spike, leaf area index, grain yield, straw yield, and biological yield, with the exception of the weight of 1000 grains. Spraying with sodium silicate had a significant impact on grain yield and harvest index but did not significantly impact the other traits. Furthermore, the interaction between irrigation and silicate application rates showed significance only for grain yield, the number of spikes/m2, and the harvest index. Applying three times irrigation could produce the highest nutrient retention, wheat yield, and water irrigation productivity. No significance was observed between 3000 m3 ha−1 and 4000 m3 ha−1 irrigation, indicating a saving of 25% of applied irrigation water. It can be concluded that applying irrigation at 3000 m3 ha−1 could be a supplemental irrigation strategy. High wheat grain yield can be achieved under deficit irrigation (3000 m3 ha−1) on the northwestern coast of Egypt with an arid climate by spraying crops with sodium silicate at a rate of 400 mg L−1.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2024-05-24","publisher":"MDPI AG","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref","Plants (Basel)","Plants, Vol 13, Iss 11, p 1462 (2024)","Plants","Volume 13","Issue 11","Pages: 1462"],"formats":["application/pdf"],"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Plants","issnPrinted":null,"issnOnline":"2223-7747","issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"1462","vol":"13","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::b59c2cf538db6f59617a3bc7a626949f","originalIds":["plants13111462","10.3390/plants13111462","50|doiboost____|b59c2cf538db6f59617a3bc7a626949f","od_______267::36cb6eff980e92095f5c6eda334c7fe6","38891271","PMC11174773","oai:pubmedcentral.nih.gov:11174773","50|od_______267::36cb6eff980e92095f5c6eda334c7fe6","oai:doaj.org/article:ab2bee0483fc4e2c80418d853b27fce3","50|doajarticles::cb1f7362401a3491daf8ca29a621d3d8","oai:mdpi.com:/2223-7747/13/11/1462/","50|multidiscipl::a15a3035cb5af70254ce33233c044d84"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3390/plants13111462"},{"scheme":"pmid","value":"388912